  "label": "The young girl is mapped as the embodiment of the stereotype that Cinco de Mayo is an excuse for white Americans to get drunk.",
  "description": "The meme uses the innocent-looking young girl as a visual anchor to represent the 'white American' who is supposedly the only one who celebrates Cinco de Mayo for the wrong reasons (to get drunk). This is a harmful analogical mapping that projects the stereotype onto the visual subject, implying that the girl represents the stereotypical white American consumer of the holiday. The juxtaposition of her innocent appearance with the hateful text amplifies the insult, making the stereotype more impactful.",
